sequencing problems”, Journal of SIAM 10, 1962): the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"least-weight Hamiltonian cycle of the simple graph, or nil when there is none; among the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optimal ones, the lexicographically least by vertex number listed from the first vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(JGraphT "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeldKarpTSP"},{"type":"text","text":"’s tour). The graph need not be complete: a missing pair is an absent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge. Tours read the simple graph, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":" documents; nil below"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"three vertices."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/shortestTour(weight:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/shortesttour(weight:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/Graph/eulerianCircuit()":{"url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/euleriancircuit()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Eulerian circuit by Hierholzer’s algorithm (Hierholzer and Wiener 1873), from the first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order with an edge; nil when the graph is not Eulerian or has no edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Circuit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has at least one). Pinned: from the current vertex the first unused edge in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order (a self-loop, twice in its row, is taken once), in the stack form","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"igraph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"igraph_eulerian_cycle"},{"type":"t